      "id": 1,
      "text": "Riversdale House Museum interprets the lives of enslaved people such as Adam Francis Plummer and the Stier and Calvert families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pgparks.com/facilities/riversdale-historic-site-museum",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Guided tours trace the plantation’s history from its 1801 construction through emancipation in 1864.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pgparks.com/facilities/riversdale-historic-site-museum",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Riverdale Park Company was founded on March 23 1889, named after the grand Federal‑style mansion that became the community’s centerpiece.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverdale_Park%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the turn of the twentieth century, Riverdale Park boasted 60 dwellings, a Presbyterian church, a schoolhouse, and a railroad station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverdale_Park%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1998 the town officially dropped the “s” and became Riverdale Park to distinguish itself from the historic plantation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverdale_Park%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Riversdale Historic Site & Museum offers free Friday tours, summer concerts, and 18th‑century cooking demos for visitors to explore the historic grounds.",
